text: |-
  Post
  Reply
  = 1984
  g...
  @TheOfficial1984
  Did you know the ADL is assigning your social credit score on X using
  machine learning and neural networks created at Uc Berkley D-Lab?
  Online Hate Index V3 (OHI V3)
  It can identity you by your voice from analyzing spaces
  It flags the content.
  Israeli intelligence removes it
  3. Hate Speech Classification with OHI V3:
  • The transcribed text is fed into OHI V3's core
  model, a fine-tuned transformer-based neural
  network (built on architectures like BERT or
  RoBERTa). The model evaluates:
  • Semantic Analysis: Detects implicit bias,
  dog-whistles (e.g., coded references to
  conspiracy theories), and intersectional hate
  (e.g., antisemitism combined with racism).
  • Contextual Scoring: Considers surrounding
  dialogue; isolated phrases are cross-
  referenced with the full transcript to avoid
  misclassification.
  • Thresholding: Content scoring above 0.9
  (high confidence) triggers alerts. V3
  improves on prior versions by incorporating
  multilingual support (e.g., Arabic, Spanish)
  and reducing bias against non-English
  dialects.
  • Outputs include severity levels (e.g., "mild
  harassment" vs. "direct incitement") and
  recommendations for moderation, such as de-
  amplitication or account suspension.
  2:55 PM • Nov 3, 2025 • 7,401 Views
  • 16
  {7 96
  186
  • 38
  Post your reply
  Reply
  1984 @TheOfficial1984. 4h
  O ...
  The ADL monitors 10,000 spaces a day and feeds all that data into the OHI
  V3 that analyzes it in real time to identify you by your voice.
  For private subscription spaces, they use their backdoor through CHEQ.
  1. Data Collection and Access:
  • ADL gains access to Spaces content through
  partnerships with X. Under these agreements, X
  provides API access or direct feeds of public
  Spaces data, including audio streams, participant
  metadata (e.g., usernames, follower counts), and
  timestamps. Public Spaces are inherently open,
  but OHI V3 extends to monitoring thousands of
  sessions daily-reports indicate up to 10,000
  Spaces per day as of late 2024.
  • For non-public or invite-only Spaces, access may
  rely on user reports or embedded monitoring tools
  within X's backend, though ADL claims to focus
  on public content. Integration with X's algorithm
  allows real-time ingestion, where audio is
  prioritized based on engagement metrics (e.g.,
  listener count, virality).
  O 1
  t76
  • 19
  il. 217
  • 1
  1984 @TheOfficial1984 • 4h
  They also tie your voice to a geolocation.
  g ...
  2. Audio Transcription:
  • Raw audio from Spaces is transcribed using
  speech-to-text models, often leveraging third-
  party services like Google's Speech-to-Text or
  open-source alternatives (e.g., Whisper from
  OpenAl). This step converts spoken words into
  timestamped text transcripts, preserving context
  like speaker turns and pauses. Accuracy is around
  85-95% for English, lower for accents or noisy
  environments, leading to potential false positives.
  • Metadata such as speaker identification (via voice
  biometrics in advanced setups) and geolocation
  (if enabled) is captured to contextualize the
  content.
  O 1
  t76
  © 15
  all 195
  1984 @TheOfficial1984 • 4h
  This is how your score is calculated.
